<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Climb</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Thief (guild level 0), Assassin (guild level 0)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>climb &lt;direction&gt;
climb up
</pre>
<p>Some ways can't be walked, only climbed: a cliff, a rope, a tree, a steep 
wall. To go that way, climb in its direction; on an ordinary way, climb 
tells you to just walk. Each climb takes 6 endurance, and you need at least 10 to try.
</p><p>Your skill and your dexterity decide it, against how hard the climb is. If 
you fail, you slip and fall, and the worse you fail, the more it hurts. 
Climbing drunk is much harder. You can't climb while inside something, 
such as a boat or a wagon, and a closed door stops you.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Dexterity</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Thieves</a>
</pre>




</div>